  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, undergoes two reversible processes, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> followed by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>, as shown below. If the work done by the gas in the two processes are same, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/b3bdc189-7931-4ec2-bb46-c10b595deea3-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 210px;\" /></p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi></math> : internal energy, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>:</mo></math> entropy, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>:</mo></math> pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>:</mo></math> volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> : gas constant)&nbsp;</p><p>(Given: molar heat capacity at constant volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub></math> of the gas is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><strong>Process -I:</strong> Adiabatic reversible process.</p><p>(Since entropy is constant)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;U</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>450</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2250</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p><strong>Process II:</strong> Isothermal reversible process.</p><p>(since internal energy is constant and entropy is increased)</p><p>Work done:</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable equalcolumns=\"true\" equalrows=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>II</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>nRTln</mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>II</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>nRTln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>II</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>Rln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>II</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>Rln</mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>nRT</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>450</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>nRT</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nRT</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p>Given</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi>II</mi></msub></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1800</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
